---
import LegalLayout from "@layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@data/site";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How LeadOrbiq handles information related to the Chrome extension and this website."
  pathname="/privacy-policy/"
  lastUpdated="August 1, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how LeadOrbiq ("we," "us," or "the extension") handles information
    in connection with the LeadOrbiq Chrome extension and this website. It's written to reflect
    what's currently confirmed about the product. Sections that depend on implementation details not
    yet verified are marked <strong>[VERIFY]</strong> and will be finalized before the extension's public
    launch — see the note at the end of this policy.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What LeadOrbiq is</h2>
  <p>
    LeadOrbiq is a Chrome extension designed to help users collect and organize business lead
    information while researching prospects, primarily through Google Maps. It is not a standalone
    web application.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information the extension may handle</h2>
  <p>
    In the course of helping you collect and organize business information from Google Maps,
    LeadOrbiq may process publicly visible business listing details (such as business name and
    category) that you choose to collect during your research. The complete, confirmed list of data
    fields the extension collects will be published on the <a href="/features/">Features page</a> and
    kept in sync with this policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>[VERIFY]</strong> Whether additional fields (such as phone numbers, websites, ratings, or
    email addresses) are collected, and the exact source of any such data, has not been confirmed for
    publication yet.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Account information</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>[VERIFY]</strong> Whether creating an account is required to use LeadOrbiq, and what account
    information (such as an email address) would be collected, has not been confirmed yet.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How information is stored</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>[VERIFY]</strong> Whether collected lead data is stored locally in your browser, synced to
    a cloud account, or both, has not been confirmed yet. This section will describe the actual storage
    behavior once verified against the current extension release.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>[VERIFY]</strong> Specific data retention periods have not been confirmed yet.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>[VERIFY]</strong> Any third-party processors, analytics tools, or payment processors used
    in connection with LeadOrbiq have not been confirmed for publication yet. We will not claim "we never
    share data with third parties" or similar blanket statements until that claim can be technically verified.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Chrome extension permissions</h2>
  <p>
    Chrome extensions must declare the permissions they request. Review the permissions listed on
    the LeadOrbiq Chrome Web Store listing before installing. <strong>[VERIFY]</strong> A plain-language
    explanation of each requested permission, matched to the current extension release, will be added
    here once confirmed.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your responsibilities</h2>
  <p>
    If you use LeadOrbiq to collect information about businesses for outreach purposes, you are
    responsible for using that information lawfully. This includes following applicable privacy and
    marketing laws, respecting Google Maps' and any other platform's terms of use, identifying
    yourself accurately, personalizing your outreach, avoiding spam, and honoring opt-out requests.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    LeadOrbiq is intended for business and professional use and is not directed at children. We do
    not knowingly collect personal information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Data requests</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a question about data handled in connection with LeadOrbiq, or want to submit a
    privacy request, use the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> and select "Privacy request" as the
    topic. We aim to respond promptly. <strong>[VERIFY]</strong> A formal data-deletion request process
    will be documented here once finalized.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy as the product and its verified capabilities change. Material
    changes will be reflected in the "Last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}
      >{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a
    >
    or through the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>A note on verification</h2>
  <p>
    Sections marked <strong>[VERIFY]</strong> reflect real gaps in what's been confirmed about the product's
    current implementation, not placeholder filler. This policy will be reviewed against actual extension
    behavior, and by qualified legal counsel, before LeadOrbiq's public launch — see
    <code>docs/09-VERIFICATION-AND-LAUNCH-CHECKLIST.md</code> in the project repository.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
